OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789410880
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/21
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A union leader has described as
OL,6, "outrageous" comments made by the
OL,7, employment minister about a pay rise
OL,8, this winter.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FMr Kenneth Clarke has said the current
OL,11,Flevel of inflation meant nobody needed
OL,12,Fa pay rise to maintain living
OL,13,Fstandards.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FBut Mr John Edmonds, of the General,
OL,16,FMunicipal, Boilermakers and Allied
OL,17,FTrades Union, said tax cuts were
OL,18,Fhelping high income earners, but the
OL,19,Fstandard of living for people on low
OL,20,Fpay was deteriorating.
OL,21,F
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 14-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789410880
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/21
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A man has been shot dead in Belfast,
OL,6, the second fatal shooting in the city
OL,7, in less than 12 hours.
OL,9,FIn the latest incident, gunmen opened
OL,10,Ffire on a police and army patrol. In a
OL,11,Ffollow-up operation by the security
OL,12,Fforces, a man was shot dead.
OL,13,         F
OL,14,FLocal people who said they saw the
OL,15,Fincident have disputed the version of
OL,16,Fevents given by the security forces -
OL,17,Fthat the man was shot by a soldier
OL,18,Fafter being challenged twice.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FThe IRA says it shot prominent loyalist
OL,21,FMr John Bingham in north Belfast early
OL,22,Ftoday. Two men are helping police with
OL,23,Ftheir enquiries.     D]CFrom 14-09-86
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789410880
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/21
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Three policemen have been seriously
OL,6, injured by a bomb explosion in central
OL,7, Paris, near the Champs Elysees.
OL,9,FThe device was found in a restaurant
OL,10,Fand carried to an underground car park,
OL,11,Fwhere it blew up.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FThe blast cut power cables, leading to
OL,14,Fa rush of calls to firemen to rescue
OL,15,Fpeople stuck in lifts.
OL,17,FThere has been a wave of bombings in
OL,18,Fthe French capital in the past week, in
OL,19,Fwhich one woman died and about 60
OL,20,Fpeople were injured.
OL,21,B
OL,23,T]CFrom 14-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11807
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789410880
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/21
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, All foreigners visiting France except
OL,6, EEC and Swiss citizens will need to
OL,7, have visas under one of a number of
OL,8, new anti-terrorist measures.
OL,10,FThe move was announced by Prime
OL,11,FMinister Chirac after the latest in a
OL,12,Fseries of bomb attacks in Paris.
OL,14,FThe visa requirement is expected to
OL,15,Flast for six months.
OL,17,FIn addition, 1,000 French soldiers are
OL,18,Fbeing assigned to strengthen frontier
OL,19,Fsecurity.
OL,23,T]CFrom 14-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11808
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789410880
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/21
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The American journalist, Mr Nicholas
OL,6, Daniloff, has been speaking about his
OL,7, two weeks' detention in Moscow.
OL,9,FMr Daniloff denied he had been under
OL,10,Finstructions from any US government
OL,11,Fagency, but would not discuss details
OL,12,Fof the charges of espionage brought
OL,13,Fagainst him by the Soviet Union.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FHe said there was no doubt he had been
OL,16,Fdetained as a result of the arrest in
OL,17,FNew York of Gennady Zakharov, who was
OL,18,Freleased from prison at the same time.
OL,19,F
OL,20,S/FA former CIA agent who defected to
OL,21,Fthe Soviet Union, Edward Lee Howard,
OL,22,Fhas appeared on Soviet TV to denounce
OL,23,FUS espionage activities.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11809
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789410880
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/21
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Social Democrats have approved a
OL,6, policy calling for the cancellation of
OL,7, the planned Trident nuclear missile
OL,8, system.
OL,10,FThe motion passed at the SDP conference
OL,11,Fin Harrogate also called for a stronger
OL,12,FEuropean role in NATO.
OL,14,FThe SDP's approval for a stronger
OL,15,Fcontribution to NATO falls short of
OL,16,Fcalling for a replacement for Polaris.
OL,18,FBut it urges an investigation into the
OL,19,Fpracticalities of building a minimum
OL,20,Fnuclear deterrent in co-operation with
OL,21,Fthe French.
OL,23,T]CFrom 14-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11810
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789410880
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0 SDP G10/21
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 CONFERENCE
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, The Social Democrat Party has rejected
OL,6, any commitment to renationalise British
OL,7, Telecom and British Gas.
OL,9,FDelegates at the Harrogate conference
OL,10,Fvoted by 154 to 84 against a proposal
OL,11,Fleaving the way clear for possible
OL,12,Ffuture renationalisation.
OL,14,FThe motion was defeated after economic
OL,15,Fspokesman Mr Ian Wrigglesworth warned
OL,16,Fthat it would provide damaging
OL,17,Fammunition for the Conservatives.
OL,19,FMr Wrigglesworth said the Conservatives
OL,20,Fwould interpret the proposal as a total
OL,21,Fcommitment to renationalisation.
OL,23,T]CFrom 14-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11811
